[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes the C code actually distinguishes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Enumerated by grepping the public header for entry points and the source for
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m every runtime branch:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```sh
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m grep -n ';' c_src/include/driver.h        # -> only `void driver(int x);`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m grep -rn 'if\|switch\|#ifdef\|#if \|getenv\|static ' c_src/src/driver.c   # -> no match
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Runtime options / modes / flags: none.** No setter, no global state, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `#ifdef`, no environment lookup, no `static` variable. The function is pure
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   apart from its stdout side effect, so there is no option cross-product.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Public entry points: exactly one — `driver`.** It *is* the lowest-level
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   entry point; there is no convenience wrapper layered over anything else, so
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   "test the low-level API too" collapses onto this one symbol.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Input shapes:** the single parameter is a by-value `int`. The shapes the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   code and the `%d` conversion actually treat differently are:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   * sign of the result (`-` printed or not) — flips at `x = -150`;
