[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C4  | `driver` | `x = -150` — result exactly `0` (single-digit, no sign) | fixed | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C5  | `driver` | `x = -149` / `x = -151` — one step either side of the zero result (`2` and `-2`, sign appears) | fixed | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C6  | `driver` | `x` chosen so the result has exactly `d` decimal digits, for every `d ∈ 1..=10`, both signs | seeded per digit count | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C7  | `driver` | mid-range positive `x ∈ [1000, INT_MAX/2 - 1]`, no overflow | 500 seeded values | [x] |
